ac173b8c292c7771db03c5306236e613d7c6f017f5d35e3c3d024b" "q-94253/selection/0a51961f309135f0f31136a649e2dfaef3357dd3a1ccf2fe4f128977cfcad042" "q-94253/selection/fccecad239f7ef7719e08e95715173591401bdaa582b3479a3aee475f3a667eb" "q-94253/selection/8da232791206fb0cb93a7d344466982ee17adaffefd9e059b336bfb49455d6e8" "q-94253/selection/c16f7f3e4fb668806294a6a99b33272cce1bb80f34e521b3aef141966167d2cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94253" :question/id #uuid "56b63b2e-bce6-5954-b2cf-7c7e968ebac3" :question/math-academy-id "q-94253" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & \\,∗\\, \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\,∗\\, \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & 0 & \\,∗\\,\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ shown above. Given that $A=PD{P}^{T}$ is an orthogonal diagonalization of a $3\\times 3$ symmetric matrix $A$ for some diagonal matrix $D,$ which of the following could be the third column of the matrix $P?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable if there exists an orthogonal matrix $P$ such that\n\n$$\nA=PD{P}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a diagonal matrix.\n\nMoreover, a matrix $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable if and only if it is symmetric.\n\nSince  $A=PD{P}^{T}$ is an orthogonal diagonalization of a $3\\times 3$ symmetric matrix $A,$ the matrix $P$ must be a $3\\times 3$ orthogonal matrix. This means that \n\n- the third column must be orthogonal to the first and second columns, and\n\n- the norm of the third column must be equal to $1.$\n\nAmong the given options, only the vector $[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]$ has both properties." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94253/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77a2b06b-e239-59a5-8af0-6cbbf27c3c08"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94253"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94257/selection/7470c38fb1111dc3239f2b2c518048d743fb7d7b66418f39282946d4f3732941" :answer/id #uuid "02a6b548-336d-5a70-8648-f4627742f230" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94257/selection/372867d69135ef136c9b0641c372d79baf65e175f6ed27792b4108746c3841f2" :answer/id #uuid "1c19e650-d767-51d8-af9e-e4fc3a0e6e36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94257/selection/35f0c5b5fd60de2a4ee8bf23506c62bb497a9116b1918543244914b62c5cc974" :answer/id #uuid "26df6e0f-9703-55cd-869a-4d7875135031" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94257/selection/9681c66d67f56e86e43c5a20c257ce3990a288b1c5af83be3ea60893d488682e" :answer/id #uuid "019ad869-da9d-51c2-bac4-c7aac854f7d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94257/selection/0518bd170ae4aae460d736ff822537cd09066fbde8a5136ff0b9c1d8d95f1f28" :answer/id #uuid "97d9ae48-0408-552a-a241-18bcf16ba094" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94257/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd914366-82fa-58dd-a662-187a577dcf82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94257/selection/9681c66d67f56e86e43c5a20c257ce3990a288b1c5af83be3ea60893d488682e" :answer-field/choices ["q-94257/selection/7470c38fb1111dc3239f2b2c518048d743fb7d7b66418f39282946d4f3732941" "q-94257/selection/372867d69135ef136c9b0641c372d79baf65e175f6ed27792b4108746c3841f2" "q-94257/selection/35f0c5b5fd60de2a4ee8bf23506c62bb497a9116b1918543244914b62c5cc974" "q-94257/selection/9681c66d67f56e86e43c5a20c257ce3990a288b1c5af83be3ea60893d488682e" "q-94257/selection/0518bd170ae4aae460d736ff822537cd09066fbde8a5136ff0b9c1d8d95f1f28"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94257" :question/id #uuid "79bb35b5-15bf-5825-9442-a19c88e03d61" :question/math-academy-id "q-94257" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. \nGiven that $D={P}^{T}\\,AP,$ where $P$ is an orthogonal matrix, which of the following could be the first column of the matrix $P?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable if there exists an orthogonal matrix $P$ such that\n\n$$\nA=PD{P}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a diagonal matrix. Equivalently,\n\n$$\nD={P}^{T}AP.\n$$\n\nMoreover, a matrix $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable if and only if it is symmetric.\n\nFirst, note that $A$ is symmetric and $D$ is diagonal. Therefore, $D={P}^{T}\\,AP$ gives an orthogonal diagonalization of $A.$\n\nFrom the diagonal matrix $D$ we deduce that the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=0,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=3.$ So, the first column of $P$ corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=0.$ \n\nNow, we need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to ${\\lambda }_{1}=0.$ Computing $A-0I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-0I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]-0[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-0I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector \n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $‖{v}_{1}‖=\\sqrt{3}.$ Dividing ${v}_{1}$ by its norm, we obtain the first column of $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94257/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "611af093-6621-5224-af2a-f769c7c0e691"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94257"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-94260"] :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. \nGiven that $D={P}^{T}\\,AP,$ where $P$ is an orthogonal matrix, which of the following could be the third column of the matrix $P?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable if there exists an orthogonal matrix $P$ such that\n\n$$\nA=PD{P}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a diagonal matrix. Equivalently,\n\n$$\nD={P}^{T}AP.\n$$\n\nMoreover, a matrix $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable if and only if it is symmetric.\n\nFirst, note that $A$ is symmetric and $D$ is diagonal. Therefore, $D={P}^{T}\\,AP$ gives an orthogonal diagonalization of $A.$\n\nFrom the diagonal matrix $D$ we deduce that the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=0,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=3.$ So, the third column of $P$ corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{3}=3.$ \n\nNow, we need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to ${\\lambda }_{3}=3.$ Computing $A-3I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-3I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-3I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector \n\n$$\n{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $‖{v}_{3}‖=\\sqrt{6}.$ Dividing ${v}_{3}$ by its norm, we obtain the third column of $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{3}}{‖{v}_{3}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-94300/selection/99227ab0eb9e2a59dc7affc81c8eebc807815c09a82206500a8b4b2d5fb89666" :answer/id #uuid "81681d67-af48-5a1c-8563-012a883f5138" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94300/selection/70acd5a3019687bb9507e72ddd06c273a6ae7e1a1e6e7d5a82dc579d7c31be8a" :answer/id #uuid "9f31307f-9d4f-5ce7-a378-67b6b7248dde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94300/selection/3d42d77764491e73541df274ce143d7a1aaea802736d20e1f8ece5616fa842b7" :answer/id #uuid "7885db70-5874-5c2f-8526-d830a01c82b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94300/selection/be1a8cfd85417c6150ce8b07dba6617ed85935b4ef146e1290c8e6b2d1280b0a" :answer/id #uuid "3b2139c0-a1dd-5f6a-ab9f-4075e889640c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94300/selection/545d473cb0bbbc06a0e28a1e8cfe08bedd11e9b717f295cb914fea8d3077d4f0" :answer/id #uuid "e6a16c61-3d62-5ddc-a684-48ccedad6949" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94300/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "420f31ca-27dd-532a-9ac5-2c510ed618f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94300/selection/99227ab0eb9e2a59dc7affc81c8eebc807815c09a82206500a8b4b2d5fb89666" :answer-field/choices ["q-94300/selection/99227ab0eb9e2a59dc7affc81c8eebc807815c09a82206500a8b4b2d5fb89666" "q-94300/selection/70acd5a3019687bb9507e72ddd06c273a6ae7e1a1e6e7d5a82dc579d7c31be8a" "q-94300/selection/3d42d77764491e73541df274ce143d7a1aaea802736d20e1f8ece5616fa842b7" "q-94300/selection/be1a8cfd85417c6150ce8b07dba6617ed85935b4ef146e1290c8e6b2d1280b0a" "q-94300/selection/545d473cb0bbbc06a0e28a1e8cfe08bedd11e9b717f295cb914fea8d3077d4f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94300" :question/id #uuid "d890c24a-d415-54d7-abf5-c338e1a2475e" :question/math-academy-id "q-94300" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. \nGiven that $D={P}^{T}\\,AP,$ where $P$ is an orthogonal matrix, which of the following could be the first column of the matrix $P?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a matrix $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable if there exists an orthogonal matrix $P$ such that\n\n$$\nA=PD{P}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a diagonal matrix. Equivalently,\n\n$$\nD={P}^{T}AP.\n$$\n\nMoreover, a matrix $A$ is orthogonally diagonalizable if and only if it is symmetric.\n\nFirst, note that $A$ is symmetric and $D$ is diagonal. Therefore, $D={P}^{T}\\,AP$ gives an orthogonal diagonalization of $A.$\n\nFrom the diagonal matrix $D$ we deduce that the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=0,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=8.$ So, the first column of $P$ corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3.$ \n\nNow, we need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3.$ Computing $A-(-3)I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-3)I & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]-(-3)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-(-3)I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector \n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $‖{v}_{1}‖=\\sqrt{11}.$ Dividing ${v}_{1}$ by its norm, we obtain the first column of $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94300/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "611af093-6621-5224-af2a-f769c7c0e691"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94300"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94262/selection/1edc2eb7198ff68262f92ba724485ecc29752578cea712c37e3c130221357cd1" :answer/id #uuid "bd7fcd73-146b-5017-a24f-4fa28f166c08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94262/selection/a3201b610977884a28fbfa9dc081ffcf41554b6e508c06b0367c42b936cc6bc0" :answer/id #uuid "aeef2a98-05d6-5b72-978e-58b4cd0e1ca8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94262/selection/478c1c7ac5d2579340e1339b08305cbe2d9d230ba4854ea60febde627f337d34" :answer/id #uuid "30963599-3032-5b8c-adcb-92ef1c6c9c7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}